If your domain uses another registrar and has the default Scaleway NS, you have to **update the DS record at your registrar**.

USAGE:
  scw domain domain enable-dnssec [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  domain                              The domain name to enable DNSSEC for.
  [ds-record.key-id]                  The key tag of the DS record.
  [ds-record.algorithm]               The cryptographic algorithm of the DNSKEY used for the DS record. (rsamd5 | dh | dsa | rsasha1 | dsa_nsec3_sha1 | rsasha1_nsec3_sha1 | rsasha256 | rsasha512 | ecc_gost | ecdsap256sha256 | ecdsap384sha384 | ed25519 | ed448)
  [ds-record.digest.type]             The digest type of the DS record. (sha_1 | sha_256 | gost_r_34_11_94 | sha_384)
  [ds-record.digest.digest]           The digest string of the DS record.
  [ds-record.digest.public-key.key]   The public key string.
  [ds-record.public-key.key]          The public key string.

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for enable-dnssec
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
